    "edgar_concentrations": {
      "filing_type": "10-Q",
      "filing_date": "2026-10-30",
      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/97210/000119312526441091/ter-20260927.htm",
      "excerpt": "The market for our test products is concentrated with a limited number of significant customers accounting for a substantial portion of the purchases of test equipment. A few customers drive significant demand for our products both through direct sales and sales to the customer’s supply partners. We expect that sales of our test products will continue to be concentrated with a limited number of significant customers for the foreseeable future. Our Semiconductor Test segment revenue exceeded $1.0 billion for the third consecutive quarter and increased 77% year over year, driven primarily by sustained demand in Artificial Intelligence (“AI”) applications across compute, memory and storage markets. In memory, revenue reached a record $301 million, marking the fourth consecutive quarter above $200 million, reflecting strong demand. Within the Product Test Group, revenue was $138 million, up 56% year over year, reflecting broad-based growth tied to AI infrastructure build-outs across board test, optical and high-speed interconnect applications, including the addition of the MultiLane Test Products joint venture. Robotics achieved profitability in the quarter on $96 million of revenue, the highest third quarter revenue in the segment’s history. Electronics and semiconductor customers represented Robotics' largest end-market during the quarter. Looking ahead, we see significant future opportunities, and we are committed to reinvesting in the business, particularly in research and development, to enable continued growth in 2027. On October 6, 2026, we entered into a securities purchase agreement and a collaboration agreement with FormFactor, Inc. (“FormFactor”), a provider of semiconductor test and measurement technologies. Under the securities purchase agreement, we agreed to make a $300.0 million minority, non-controlling equity investment in FormFactor. The transaction is expected to close within the fourth quarter of 2026, subject to customary closing conditions and regulatory approvals. Under the collaboration agreement, we and FormFactor will collaborate on joint solutions that combine our test platforms with FormFactor’s probe, contactor, and interface technologies to help semiconductor customers accelerate device validation and bring advanced devices to production, including in silicon photonics, high-performance compute, advanced packaging, and high-bandwidth memory. On April 8, 2026, we and HTP Holding SAL (“MultiLane”) formed a joint venture, MultiLane Test Products Holding LLC (“MLTP”), to which MultiLane contributed the assets of its test and measurement business.",
      "note": "未命中『accounted for X% of revenue/receivable』specific 句型，改取全文第一個含 concentrat 字串的段落——本檔可能未逐條揭露單一客戶營收集中度，writer 需自行判讀此段是否足以回答客戶集中度問題（也可能代表該公司客戶分散無須揭露）"
    },
